course: dictionary
lesson: 10101
title: Thin: many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word thin has several meanings, and the words around it show you which one you need. «A frog can take in some oxygen through its thin, moist skin.» Here thin describes skin, so it means not thick: there is only a small distance between the two sides.
explain: Look at what thin describes. A thin person has little fat on the body. A thin liquid flows easily, like water. Thin hair or trees are not close together. Try each meaning in the sentence and see which one still makes sense.
explain: Thin can also be a verb, an action word. To thin something is to make it thinner or weaker, as when you add water to thin a sauce. The endings help too: thins, thinned and thinning all show an action.
fact: Thin means having a small distance between its two sides, like thin paper.
fact: «Thin air» is low in oxygen, as on high mountains, so climbers breathe hard.
fact: «Vanish into thin air» means disappear completely, and «thin on the ground» means few.
fact: «Skating on thin ice» means taking a risk. Stay off frozen ponds unless an adult says it is safe.
fact: Thin can describe a thing (thin paper), a person or animal (a thin cat), or a liquid that flows easily.
exercise: «A frog can take in some oxygen through its thin, moist skin.» What does thin mean here? | A thin person with little fat on the body | A thin liquid that flows like water | To make something weaker | *Not thick, with a small distance between its two sides
exercise: «Darwin's finches have beaks shaped for different foods, thick for seeds and thin for insects.» What is the opposite of thin in this sentence? | Short | Heavy | *Thick | Sharp
exercise: Jayden says «vanish into thin air» means the air is thin. What does the phrase mean? | Breathe hard on a mountain | *Disappear completely | Fly up into the sky | Become very cold
test: What does thin mean in «a thin dull layer» on a brass door knob? | To make something weaker | Thin air high up on a mountain | *Having little thickness | A thin person
test: In cooking, what does «to thin a sauce» mean? | Cook it until it is hard | Make it very hot | Put it in the fridge | *Add water so it is less thick
exam: «Skating on thin ice» means what? | *Taking a risk | Walking on a frozen pond with an adult | Skating on a sunny day | Skating very fast on a frozen pond
